{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-83746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are discrete random variables?\n\n- The number of hearts in a standard deck of cards\n- The number of diamonds obtained when $7$ cards are randomly selected from a standard deck of cards\n- The number of times a card is selected from a standard deck of cards until a King appears" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041842/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38ac0a7329523615058c6edd535db9049d09c549047084033bba41733014794"} {"question" "q-83746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\nA *discrete* random variable is a random variable\n\n- that has finitely many possible values, or\n\n- whose possible values can be listed in a sequence: ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},…$\n\nRemember that a real interval (e.g. $(a,b)$ or $[a,b]$) cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a discrete random variable. The number of hearts in a particular complete deck of cards is not the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\n- Statement II describes a discrete random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values can be listed in a sequence: $0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7.$\n\n- Statement III describes a discrete random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and we can count its possible values in a sequence: $1,2,3,…$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041842/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38ac0a7329523615058c6edd535db9049d09c549047084033bba41733014794"} {"question" "q-83746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041842/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "98770bd42e2537445ea14aada000eb543290c5d4c0f5a9f71aa70e83ef6a4907"} {"question" "q-83746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041842/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38ac0a7329523615058c6edd535db9049d09c549047084033bba41733014794"} {"question" "q-83746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041842/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38ac0a7329523615058c6edd535db9049d09c549047084033bba41733014794"} {"question" "q-83746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041842/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38ac0a7329523615058c6edd535db9049d09c549047084033bba41733014794"} {"question" "q-83761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are discrete random variables?\n\n- The weight of a randomly selected student\n- The amount of water in a randomly selected student's water bottle\n- The number of books borrowed by a randomly selected library user in a particular month" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041842/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38ac0a7329523615058c6edd535db9049d09c549047084033bba41733014794"} {"question" "q-83761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\nA *discrete* random variable is a random variable\n\n- that has finitely many possible values, or\n\n- whose possible values can be listed in a sequence: ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},…$\n\nRemember that a real interval (e.g. $(a,b)$ or $[a,b]$) cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a discrete random variable. Although its value is determined by the result of an experiment, the possible values are real numbers that cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\n- Statement II does *not* describe a discrete random variable. Although its value is determined by the result of an experiment, we cannot list the possible real-numbered values in a sequence.\n\n- Statement III describes a discrete random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and it has finitely many possible values: $0,1,2,3,…$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041842/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38ac0a7329523615058c6edd535db9049d09c549047084033bba41733014794"} {"question" "q-83761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041842/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "98770bd42e2537445ea14aada000eb543290c5d4c0f5a9f71aa70e83ef6a4907"} {"question" "q-83761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041842/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38ac0a7329523615058c6edd535db9049d09c549047084033bba41733014794"} {"question" "q-83761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["te